  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Florida has recorded $310M in federal contract obligations for FY2027 to date. The state received 1,591 awards with an average award size of $195K. Obligations fell 99.1% year over year. The FY2027 total is partial, fiscal year to date, and follows a multi-year sequence that ran $26.6B in FY22, $29B in FY23, $31.3B in FY24, $32.5B in FY25, and $33.1B in FY26. The Department of Veterans Affairs is the largest buyer so far, obligating $192M, followed by the National Aeronautics and Space Administration with $60.8M and the Department of Homeland Security with $21.7M. Veterans Development Corporation, Inc. is the largest vendor in FY2027 to date with $63.1M in obligations, followed by BLUE ORIGIN, LLC with $46.1M. Commercial and Institutional Building Construction is the largest industry by obligations with $108M. All figures are contract obligations and current-year totals are partial because the fiscal year is still in progress.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How does FY2027 federal contracting in Florida compare to prior years?",
        "body": "Florida obligated $310M in FY2027 to date. Florida obligations followed $26.6B in FY22, $29B in FY23, $31.3B in FY24, $32.5B in FY25, and $33.1B in FY26. Florida obligations fell 99.1% year over year. The FY2027 total is partial, fiscal year to date."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and vendors dominate FY2027 Florida federal obligations?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $192M, making it the largest buyer so far in FY2027 to date. The National Aeronautics and Space Administration obligated $60.8M and the Department of Homeland Security obligated $21.7M. VETERANS DEVELOPMENT CORPORATION, INC. received $63.1M and BLUE ORIGIN, LLC received $46.1M among the top vendors. Commercial and Institutional Building Construction leads industries with $108M in obligations."
      }
    ]
